IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcrr-core`
IMPORT `wcrr-seat`

-- Cases for the injured worker's seat of the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Regulation 2025 (Qld).
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it; none is
-- copied from the encoding's output. Edges: each threshold, the last day of each period, one past each cap.
-- QOTE for 2026-27 is $1,994.50 (QOTE Notice 2026). Calendar: 7 September 2026 is a Monday; 1 October 2026 a Thursday.

`3 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 9 2026
`7 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 7 9 2026
`1 Sep 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2026
`1 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026
`1 Oct 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025
`1 Sep 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025
`30 Jun 2027` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027
`1 Jul 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2027
`unused day`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 15 -- the excess period amount`

-- The lesser of QOTE ($1,994.50) and the weekly payment.
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Sep 2026` 0 1500 EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Sep 2026` 0 2100 EQUALS JUST 1994.50
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Sep 2026` 0 1994.50 EQUALS JUST 1994.50
-- Last day of 2026-27 still takes the 2026-27 QOTE; the next day has none deposited.
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `30 Jun 2027` 0 2100 EQUALS JUST 1994.50
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Jul 2027` 0 2100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- An earlier year with its QOTE given (hypothetical $1,953.70), and without it.
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Sep 2025` 1953.70 2000 EQUALS JUST 1953.70
#ASSERT `What weekly amount ends my excess period?` `1 Sep 2025` 0 2000 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 105-109 -- normal weekly earnings`

-- s 106(1): regular overtime for required work that would have continued: may be counted.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `overtime` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not regular: "only if" fails.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `overtime` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Would not have continued: fails.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `penalties` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 106(2): an excluded wages item must not be counted, whatever else holds.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `an allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Ordinary earnings: s 106 is silent.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `any other earnings` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Higher duties not for work the employer required: s 106(1) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be counted in my NWE?` `higher duties` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What is my NWE worked out from?` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the worker's own earnings in the 12 months before the injury (ss 105, 106)`
#ASSERT `What is my NWE worked out from?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `regard must be had to the NWE of a comparable person employed by the same employer (s 107(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `What is my NWE worked out from?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `regard must be had to the NWE of a comparable person employed by another employer (s 107(2)(b))`
-- s 109: the insurer's fair calculation is taken to be the NWE, even where s 107 would apply.
#ASSERT `What is my NWE worked out from?` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a calculation the insurer considers fair, which is taken to be the NWE (s 109)`
#ASSERT `Are my earnings from all my employers counted?` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are my earnings from all my employers counted?` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 113-115 -- certificates and examinations`

-- s 113(1)(b): a certificate came with the application, so s 113 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 113 does not apply: the declaration does not stand in for a medical certificate`
-- s 113(1)(c): a doctor was available.
#ASSERT `What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 113 does not apply: the declaration does not stand in for a medical certificate`
#ASSERT `What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `taken to be the certificate; the insurer may accept it as proof of incapacity for not more than 3 days`
#ASSERT `What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `taken to be the certificate, but it cannot be accepted again as proof of incapacity for an injury in this event`
#ASSERT `What does my declaration do in place of a medical certificate?` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `taken to be the certificate; for a fatal injury s 113(3) sets no limit`
-- s 113(3)(b): "not more than 3 days": 5 claimed gives 3; exactly 3 gives 3; 2 gives 2.
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS JUST 2
-- s 113(3)(a): only once per event.
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 2 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `For how many days can my declaration prove my incapacity?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS JUST 0

#ASSERT `Can a practitioner's document from outside Queensland stand in for my certificate?` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a practitioner's document from outside Queensland stand in for my certificate?` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a practitioner's document from outside Queensland stand in for my certificate?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a practitioner's document from outside Queensland stand in for my certificate?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the examination requirement properly made?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 115(4): within 10 days after an examination on 3 September 2026: 13 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the examiner report to the insurer?` `3 Sep 2026` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 13 9 2026

